[{"id":2590320728,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6aZShY","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","login":"Calinou","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou"},"body":"Tested locally on Windows 11 24H2, it works as expected.\r\n\r\nSome comments:\r\n\r\n- All instances of `extened` should be renamed to `extended`.\r\n- `list_extended_attributes()` should be renamed to `get_extended_attributes_list()`. We generally only use method names starting with `list_` for \"stateful\" approaches like `DirAccess.list_dir_begin()`.\r\n- Trying to remove a nonexistent extended attribute won't print any warning or error in output. It should probably print a warning at least.\r\n- Setting extended attributes on `project.godot` while Godot is open will make a file reload dialog show up in the editor, which I guess is expected.\r\n- Using non-ASCII characters in attribute names works correctly (on Windows at least).","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102232#pullrequestreview-2590320728","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102232","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-02-03T15:47:36Z"},{"id":2590323307,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6aZTJr","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","login":"Calinou","type":"U